erefore, substitute x = y = z into equation (1):\n\nx2 + x2 + x2 = 2x + 2 ⇒ 3x2 = 2x + 2 ⇒ 3x2 - 2x - 2 = 0\n\nSolving quadratic equation:\n\nx = [ 2 ± sqrt(4 + 24 ) ] / 6 = [ 2 ± sqrt(28 ) ] /6 = [ 2 ± 2*sqrt(7 ) ] /6 = [1 ± sqrt(7 ) ] /3\n\nTherefore, x = (1 + sqrt(7))/3 or x = (1 - sqrt(7))/3. Since points lie on the sphere radius √3 and the coordinates must be real.\n\nWe need to check which solution is valid. Let\'s compute x=(1 + sqrt(7))/3.\n\nCompute x ≈ (1 + 2.645 ) /3 ≈ 3.645 /3 ≈ 1.215, but point P is (x, x, x ), but the sphere radius is √3 ≈ 1.732. So distance from O to P is sqrt(3x2 ). If x ≈ 1.215, then 3x2 ≈ 3*(1.215)^2 ≈ 3*1.476 ≈ 4.428, so distance is sqrt(4.428 ) ≈ 2.104, which is larger than √3. Not possible.\n\nThe other solution x=(1 - sqrt(7))/3 ≈ (1 - 2.645)/3 ≈ -1.645/3 ≈ -0.5483. Then distance from O is sqrt( 3*( (-0.5483 )^2 )) ≈ sqrt(3*0.3009 )≈ sqrt(0.9027 )≈ 0.95. Yes, this is less than √3 ≈ 1.732, so possible.\n\nTherefore, x = (1 - sqrt(7))/3 ≈ -0.5483.\n\nTherefore, coordinates of P are ( (1 - sqrt(7))/3, (1 - sqrt(7))/3, (1 - sqrt(7))/3 )\n\nTherefore, center coordinates O is ( (1 - sqrt(7))/3, (1 - sqrt(7))/3, (1 - sqrt(7))/3 )\n\nNow, equation of plane ABC is needed. Points A(1,0,0 ), B(0,1,0 ), C'}]}
